{"ok": false, "issues": ["The requirement says the optional fee in lieu of a security deposit is capped at 1 month's rent 'in total with any deposit'. The source (clause (C)) caps only the total of the fee or recurring payments at 1 month's rent, regardless of lease duration or extensions. The 'in total with any deposit' wording is not supported by the source."], "fix": {"requirement": "A security deposit may not exceed the first month's rent. It must be held in a separate interest-bearing Massachusetts bank account, and the tenant must get a receipt within 30 days naming the bank, location, amount and account number. The tenant must get a signed receipt when the deposit is received, and a written statement of the premises' condition within 10 days after tenancy commences or on receipt of the deposit, whichever is later. If the lessor holds the deposit for a year or longer, it must pay interest at 5% per year (or the lesser amount actually received from the bank) at the end of each year of the tenancy. The lessor must return the deposit, less permitted deductions, within 30 days after the tenancy ends. Permitted deductions are unpaid rent or water charges, unpaid tax increases under a conforming escalation clause, and reasonable repair of damage beyond normal wear and tear. Damage deductions require a sworn itemized list with cost evidence within the same 30 days. The lessor must keep deposit records for 2 years after the tenancy ends. The deposit and accrued interest must be transferred to a successor in interest. As amended effective Aug 1, 2025, the Executive Office of Housing and Livable Communities may by regulation authorize an optional fee in lieu of a security deposit. The total of that fee or its recurring payments may not exceed 1 month's rent, regardless of lease length or extensions."}}
